WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.247 --> 00:00:01.830
JOANNA SMITH: This
week, we're talking

00:00:01.830 --> 00:00:05.910
about Data Fusion, VPC Service
Controls, and Cloud Armor.

00:00:05.910 --> 00:00:09.210
I'm Joanna Smith, and welcome
to "This Week in Cloud," where

00:00:09.210 --> 00:00:13.170
we serve you the
lowest latency news.

00:00:13.170 --> 00:00:16.740
Cloud Data Fusion is
now generally available.

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:20.430
Data Fusion is a great tool for
seasoned engineers and newbies

00:00:20.430 --> 00:00:24.540
alike, because it makes it easy
to clean, transform, and blend

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:25.410
data.

00:00:25.410 --> 00:00:27.150
Whether you're short
on data engineers,

00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:30.600
or you'd just like to make
their job a little less mundane,

00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:33.480
this tool is here to help.

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:35.490
VPC Service Controls
is a tool that

00:00:35.490 --> 00:00:38.430
allows admins to mitigate
the risk of data breaches.

00:00:38.430 --> 00:00:41.100
And now, debugging
and understanding

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:43.350
denied requests from
the tool gets simpler

00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:45.173
with unique identifiers.

00:00:45.173 --> 00:00:46.590
It's one thing to
know that you're

00:00:46.590 --> 00:00:48.660
defending against
breaches, but another

00:00:48.660 --> 00:00:50.580
to trace your way
through the logs

00:00:50.580 --> 00:00:53.260
and figure out where the
bad actors are coming from.

00:00:53.260 --> 00:00:55.800
So here's wishing
you quick resolutions

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:58.560
to your access issues.

00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:00.290
Google Cloud Armor
helps enterprises

00:01:00.290 --> 00:01:02.540
protect both themselves
and their users

00:01:02.540 --> 00:01:04.970
from DDLS and
targeted web attacks.

00:01:04.970 --> 00:01:06.920
And we're now adding
web application firewall

00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:10.280
capabilities to expand
the scope of protection,

00:01:10.280 --> 00:01:13.160
as well as custom rules, and
geobased access controls,

00:01:13.160 --> 00:01:14.060
and more.

00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:15.850
These updates are
currently in beta,

00:01:15.850 --> 00:01:19.430
so try them out, and let
us know what you think.

00:01:19.430 --> 00:01:22.070
SmallFLex, Gartner
named Google Cloud

00:01:22.070 --> 00:01:24.740
a leader in its 2019
Magic Quadrant Report

00:01:24.740 --> 00:01:27.440
for Operational Database
Management Systems.

00:01:27.440 --> 00:01:29.330
This was pretty
cool for us to hear.

00:01:29.330 --> 00:01:32.000
But what's actually really cool
is hearing that our users like

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:35.030
us, because for our team,
recognition like this

00:01:35.030 --> 00:01:36.920
reinforces that our
customers believe

00:01:36.920 --> 00:01:40.670
our databases are flexible,
open, and easy to use.

00:01:40.670 --> 00:01:42.080
And that's our priority.

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:43.520
And we do it for you all.

00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:46.897
Anytime you've got feedback to
share, we're happy to hear it.

00:01:46.897 --> 00:01:48.980
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:01:48.980 --> 00:01:51.200
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:54.390
Any thoughts or ideas, leave
us a comment or tweet us.

00:01:54.390 --> 00:01:57.280
And we'll see you in the Cloud.

